course: dictionary
lesson: 4102
title: The word girl
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A girl is a female child or a young woman. Girl is a noun, which means it names a person. Its plural is girls, so one girl becomes two or more girls.
explain: In class, people are often counted as girls and boys. Together, girls and boys make children. «A girl in Vermont plays on the icy playground» tells us one child, a girl, is the one doing things in that sentence.
explain: Look at the words around girl to understand it. «A little girl» means a young girl. «Schoolgirl» joins school and girl to mean a girl who goes to school.
fact: A girl is a female child or a young woman.
fact: The plural of girl is girls.
fact: Girls and boys together make children.
fact: «A little girl» means a young girl, and «schoolgirl» means a girl who goes to school.
fact: In «the girls' team», the apostrophe after the s shows that the team belongs to the girls.
exercise: «A girl in Dublin always left in a rush and ran across the road to catch the bus.» What is a girl? | A grown-up man | *A female child or a young woman | A male child | A kind of bus
exercise: Which word is the plural of girl? | *girls | girl | girler | girlies
exercise: Girls and boys together make what? | Schools | Teams | Adults | *Children
test: What does «schoolgirl» mean? | A bus driver for children | A teacher who runs a school | *A girl who goes to school | A type of school bag
test: Which phrase means a young girl? | the girls' team | *a little girl | a big school | a little man
exam: In «the girls' team», what does the apostrophe show? | *It shows the team belongs to the girls | It means there is only one girl in the team | It means the team is all boys | It is a spelling mistake
